  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Dl-Isoindolmycin and U373 MG through a series of target interactions. Dl-Isoindolmycin is implicated in targeting SNU-387, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (-)-Bisdechlorogeodin and Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside), both of which also target U373 MG. Additionally, SNU-387 is a target of Yuanhuapine, which also directs to U373 MG. These findings indicate that Dl-Isoindolmycin may act through a common pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of SNU-387, which in turn influences U373 MG. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a strong, albeit indirect, relationship between Dl-Isoindolmycin and U373 MG, likely mediated through SNU-387. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain, as the pathways are not fully elucidated."
